{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789917886,"nonce":"faTVBttQ8eesn+C/H/tsb2PDVZw=","title":"LLVM tier: a static Int reads back zero-extended, so `a % b` on statics gives 255","message":"`static var a:Int; static var b:Int; a = 255; b = -8; a % b` prints 255\nunder `--llvm` (7 on the tiered path). `StoreGlobal` zero-extends a narrower\nint into the i64 global slot and `LoadGlobal` handed the i64 back for an\n`i32`-typed load, so -8 arrived as 4294967288. Issue8845/Issue8849/\nIssue5289 score WRONG_ANSWER on the LLVM path for this alone. Fix: truncate\nthe loaded i64 to the load's declared int width.","files":null}]}